  "scope": "Supporting constructions for protected joining traces of the native partner reserve. The four-label original/virtual circuit construction forces selected actual crossings to be singleton primary pieces. All registered palette, trace, boundary, and star interfaces retain their explicit actual-copy, parity, regularity, disjointness, and numerical hypotheses. The final native two-pair external assembly constructs its joining palette, exact protected traces, zero-or-one-star geometry, complete exceptional extension, old-core parity, and true core-deficit loads from a safe regular residual and retained-core/numerical budgets. The precise conclusions and assumptions of each named public theorem are recorded in the proof map and semantic review. This continuation does not construct the complete native safe residual or finish the zero-/one-pair multi-star branches, terminal assembly, or the main theorem. All 69 pinned numbered records, including their 51 complete statuses, remain unchanged.",
